Ok.  An easy solution to this would be to give an "area code" as part of
the shops phone number.  Thus, Alsophs Weapon Shop: 2-333-1111 would
indicate that the shop is on level 2-xxx-xxxx and the x's could maybe
give map coordinates or some other clue.  A phone book, when found,
would generate phone numbers for shops that it knows about, Ie: current
level and above (numerically below).  Granted, it wouldn't be _as_
useful, but you have to sacrifice something...

